# Cursor Rules Index

This file provides a quick reference to all available cursorrules and their purposes.

## Always Applied Rules

These rules are automatically applied to all AI interactions:

1. **00-persona.mdc**: Core AI persona, communication style, and decision-making protocols
2. **01-ai-guidelines.mdc**: AI-GUIDELINES orchestration policy and compliance requirements
3. **byterover-rules.mdc**: ByteRover MCP knowledge management tools
4. **laravel-boost.mdc**: Laravel Boost workflow guidelines and tool usage

## Mode-Specific Rules

These rules are applied on-demand when the user requests specific expertise:

### Architect Mode (`.cursor/rules/modes/architect.mdc`)

**When to use**: System design, scalability, integration patterns, architecture documentation

**Key capabilities**:

- System architecture design
- Scalability planning
- Technology evaluation
- Integration patterns
- Risk assessment
- Architecture documentation (ADRs, diagrams)

**Activation**: "Please use architect mode" or "I need architectural guidance"

### Product Manager Mode (`.cursor/rules/modes/product-manager.mdc`)

**When to use**: PRDs, user stories, feature prioritization, roadmap planning

**Key capabilities**:

- Product Requirements Documents (PRDs)
- User story creation
- Feature prioritization
- Roadmap planning
- Success metrics definition
- Stakeholder communication

**Activation**: "Please use product manager mode" or "I need to create a PRD"

### Test Engineer Mode (`.cursor/rules/modes/tester.mdc`)

**When to use**: Test strategy, test cases, test automation, quality assurance

**Key capabilities**:

- Test strategy development
- Test case creation (unit, feature, integration, E2E, browser)
- Test automation
- Quality assurance planning
- Bug investigation
- Test coverage analysis (90% minimum)
- Performance testing

**Activation**: "Please use tester mode" or "I need help with testing"

## Quick Reference

### Common Tasks

| Task | Recommended Mode | Additional Rules |
|------|-----------------|------------------|
| Create PRD | Product Manager | - |
| Design Architecture | Architect | - |
| Implement Feature | Standard (Laravel Boost) | - |
| Create Tests | Tester | - |
| Full Feature Workflow | All modes (sequential) | - |
| Code Review | Standard | - |
| Bug Investigation | Tester | - |
| Performance Optimization | Architect + Standard | - |
| Security Review | Standard (Security guidelines) | - |

### Mode Activation Examples

```markdown
# Architect Mode

"Please use architect mode to design the system architecture"
"I need architectural guidance for scaling this application"

# Product Manager Mode

"Please use product manager mode to create a PRD"
"I need help prioritizing features - use product manager mode"

# Tester Mode

"Please use tester mode to create comprehensive tests"
"I need a test strategy - use tester mode"
```

## Rule Hierarchy

1. **Always Applied Rules** (00-persona, 01-ai-guidelines, byterover-rules, laravel-boost)
2. **Mode-Specific Rules** (activated on-demand)
3. **Project-Specific Guidelines** (AGENTS.md, AI-GUIDELINES.md)

## Compliance Checklist

All AI interactions should:

- [ ] Follow core persona and communication style
- [ ] Comply with AI-GUIDELINES orchestration policy
- [ ] Use ByteRover MCP tools appropriately
- [ ] Follow Laravel Boost workflow guidelines
- [ ] Apply mode-specific expertise when requested
- [ ] Maintain junior developer focus
- [ ] Ensure 90%+ test coverage
- [ ] Apply security principles
- [ ] Consider performance implications
- [ ] Document decisions and patterns

